    "updated_at": "2017-05-22T10:12:32Z",
    "body": "I think I prefer not fixing this. We've always regarded the `/` in `<img/>` as a talisman and we've advocated against \"polyglot\" on the basis that pretending `/` and other XML things have meaning will result in more confusion (it's much better to know `<input>` doesn't have a closing tag).\r\n\r\nThis seems more in the realm of lint tools and coding guidelines.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
